================================================================================
SWRL -> SHACL regression test coverage
================================================================================

Context:
Following the removal of the legacy SWRL engine (SHACL-AF now executes the
IF/THEN business-rules UI), we hardened the test suite with a dedicated
regression suite that pins the SWRL -> SHACL-AF behavioural contract so any
future drift away from the legacy semantics is caught. The suite complements
test_shacl_rule_engine.py (which asserts *that* SQL is emitted) by nailing
down *what* that SQL means and *what* the engine returns, across the full
capability battery (unary/binary atoms, property chains, comparison + string
built-ins, closed-world negation).

Changes:
1. tests/units/reasoning/test_swrl_to_shacl_regression.py (new, 22 tests) —
   - TestEngineContractParity: end-to-end via a canned triple store —
     `stats["phase"] == "swrl"` / `engine == "shacl-af"`, `swrl:<rule>`
     provenance, enabled-only rules_count vs rules_total, disabled rules emit
     no SQL, whole-battery error-free run, materialisation INSERT +
     `swrl:materialized` marker, focus restricts to the entity URI, and
     inference_limit is applied.
   - TestInferenceSqlSemantics: the SQL each capability compiles to —
     property-chain derives the relationship head with closed-world NOT EXISTS
     de-dup; comparison built-in classifies via rdf:type HighValue with an
     ANSI-safe TRY_CAST filter; string built-in translates `contains` to
     LIKE CONCAT without leaking the built-in predicate; class-only rule is a
     classification no-op (no inference SELECT); negation has no positive
     inference SELECT and renders its closed-world body as nested NOT EXISTS
     in the violation query.
   - TestDialectParity: across the whole battery, Postgres SQL leaks no
     Spark-only syntax (TRY_CAST / RLIKE / CURRENT_TIMESTAMP()) and Spark SQL
     leaks no Postgres-only syntax (::float8 / ::double precision).
   - TestTranspilerClassificationParity: stable sh:TripleRule vs sh:SPARQLRule
     mapping per capability, antecedent-class targeting, CONSTRUCT bodies on
     SPARQL rules, and FILTER NOT EXISTS for negation.
   - TestShaclViewParity: the new read-only SHACL view (serialize) and the
     editor preview render every capability (one sh:NodeShape per rule under a
     single shared header; preview returns well-formed turtle + rule_type).

Modified files:
- tests/units/reasoning/test_swrl_to_shacl_regression.py (new)

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m 'not scenario' -> 10184 passed, 325
skipped (the new suite adds 22). Focused business-rules run
(tests/units/reasoning + tests/units/ontology + test_routes.py +
test_swrl_text_pane.py) -> 1248 passed. The only full-suite failure is
test_size_budget.py (agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py::run_agent 198->200),
verified pre-existing and unrelated to this change.

================================================================================
If-Then rules: set-attribute (data-property) consequents
================================================================================

Context:
The IF-Then business-rules editor could only add relationships (object
properties) or class assertions in the THEN clause. Users need to *update
attributes* too — set a data (datatype) property to a value, e.g.
"IF Customer(?x) AND hasScore(?x,?s) AND swrlb:greaterThan(?s, 500) THEN
priority(?x, "high")". Previously a literal in a consequent object position was
silently dropped (the flat SQL backend emitted '' for any non-variable object).
Semantics chosen: literal constant value with REPLACE (a true update — any
existing value for that property on the entity is removed and the new one set).
Design spec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-08-ifthen-set-attribute-design.md.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/reasoning/shacl_rules/ShaclFlatSqlBackend.py — teach the
   consequent renderer that a 2-arg atom's object may be a literal:
   - new module helpers `_literal_object_sql` (SQL literal for a non-variable
     object, else None), `_has_literal_assignment`, and
     `_consequent_inference_selects` / `_consequent_materialize_stmts`
     (extracted the per-consequent-atom SELECT / INSERT-DELETE rendering out of
     the two long builder methods).
   - inference SELECT emits the literal object with exact (s,p,o) de-dup, so a
     set-attribute fires when the current value differs and no-ops when equal.
   - materialisation emits DELETE (existing subject+predicate) then INSERT —
     the replace update. Relationship/class consequents are unchanged.
   - inference/materialisation guards relaxed so a class-only antecedent
     (e.g. Customer(?x) -> priority(?x,"high")) is realisable from the class
     anchor alone, while a class consequent without props stays a no-op.
2. src/back/core/reasoning/shacl_rules/SwrlToShaclTranspiler.py — the TripleRule
   Turtle branch now emits `sh:object "<literal>"` for a literal consequent
   (was hard-coded `sh:object sh:this`). CONSTRUCT head already rendered the
   literal via `_term`.
3. src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_business_rules.html — new
   "Set attributes" section in the THEN pane (mirrors the IF attribute
   conditions): entity + data-property dropdowns + value input.
4. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-swrl.js — `assignments` state +
   `_assignmentAtoms()` (builds property(?subj, "literal") consequent atoms),
   `addAssignmentRow` / `_removeAssignment` / `_onAssignmentChange` /
   `_renderAssignments`; `_updateRulePane` and `saveRule` fold assignments into
   the consequent and the live SHACL preview; `_prefillFromRule` parses
   literal-object consequent atoms back into assignment rows (round-trip, no
   read-only flip); `_resetEditor` clears the rows.
5. Tests:
   - tests/units/reasoning/test_swrl_to_shacl_regression.py — added SET_ATTRIBUTE
     to the battery + a TestSetAttribute class (inference literal + exact dedup,
     numeric literal unquoted, materialise DELETE-then-INSERT, conditional guard
     retained, relationship consequent unchanged, transpiler TripleRule
     `sh:object "high"`, end-to-end provenance).
   - tests/units/front/test_swrl_text_pane.py — contract for the "Set
     attributes" section markup + the new SwrlModule helpers.
6. tests/units/architecture/baseline.json — after extracting the two renderers,
   build_inference_sql shrank 165->118 (updated) and build_materialization_sql
   dropped below budget (entry removed); the ShaclFlatSqlBackend class stays
   under 800 LOC.
7. docs/user-guide.md — documented the THEN "Set attributes" step.

